# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hive Authority Kernel — environment reference
# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in. NEVER commit real tokens.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Gateway (HTTP API on :8787) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# HIVE_API_HOST / HIVE_API_PORT      — bind address (default 0.0.0.0:8787)
# HIVE_DB_PATH                       — SQLite WAL path (default .hive/live.db)
# HIVE_GATEWAY_TOKEN                 — coarse outer bearer (optional network edge).
#                                      When set, every /api/* except GET /api/health
#                                      requires: Authorization: Bearer <token>.
#                                      Carries NO principal identity — hst_ sessions do.
# HIVE_GATEWAY_TOKEN=
# HIVE_ADMIN_TOKEN                   — >=32 chars. REQUIRED when NODE_ENV=production or
#                                      HIVE_REQUIRE_ADMIN=1. Gates POST /api/session/mint,
#                                      POST /api/session/revoke (revoke-all) and /api/reset.
#                                      Dev convenience: when unset, these are open (with a
#                                      boot warning); always set it before network exposure.
# HIVE_ADMIN_TOKEN=
# HIVE_MASTER_KEY                    — 32 bytes, base64 (`openssl rand -base64 32`). REQUIRED
#                                      when NODE_ENV=production or HIVE_REQUIRE_ADMIN=1.
#                                      AES-256-GCM custodial-key envelope encryption
#                                      (principal.privkey, authority_meta.gateway_priv).
#                                      Legacy plaintext rows re-encrypt automatically at boot.
#                                      Dev-only example (DO NOT use in prod):
#                                      aGl2ZS1kZXYtbWFzdGVyLWtleS1kby1ub3QtdXNlcDE=
# HIVE_MASTER_KEY=
# HIVE_GATEWAY_SIGNING_KEY           — base64url Ed25519 PKCS8 DER. When set, overrides the
#                                      custodial gateway_priv for signing (KMS/HSM-backed env).
# HIVE_GATEWAY_SIGNING_KEY=
# HIVE_DEV_INSECURE_ACTOR=1          — local-dev ONLY: HTTP routes trust body/query `actor`
#                                      without a session. NEVER set in shared/prod (boot
#                                      refuses in production).
# HIVE_ENABLE_DEV_DRILLS=1           — enables POST /api/scenario and /api/reset (off by
#                                      default; /api/reset additionally requires HIVE_ADMIN_TOKEN)
# HIVE_REQUIRE_ADMIN=1               — enforce admin-token boot checks outside production
# HIVE_ALLOWED_ORIGINS               — comma-separated CORS allowlist (default: loopback only).
#                                      Allow-Origin is reflected only for matches; Authorization
#                                      is in Allow-Headers.
# HIVE_ALLOWED_HOSTS                 — comma-separated Host allowlist; mismatches get 421
#                                      (default: any — set this in production; GET /api/health exempt)

# ── Effect integrations (outbox: open-pr, merge, post-github, open-branch, post-slack)
# HIVE_INTEGRATIONS=auto             — auto | live | simulation
#   auto        : live per category when credentials resolve, else simulation (default)
#   live        : hard-fail at boot unless BOTH GitHub and Slack resolve
#   simulation  : in-memory simulated connectors only (never hits the network)
# HIVE_EFFECT_LEDGER                 — ledger path (default .hive/live-ledger.jsonl)

# GitHub (outbox effects open-pr / merge / post-github / open-branch)
# HIVE_GITHUB_REPO=owner/name        — target repository, REQUIRED for live GitHub
# HIVE_GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...          — PAT or fine-grained token
# HIVE_GITHUB_USE_GH_CLI=1           — opt in to the `gh auth token` fallback (default: OFF)
# HIVE_GITHUB_API_URL=https://api.github.com          — override for GitHub Enterprise / tests
# HIVE_GITHUB_REPO=acme/www
# HIVE_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ── Inbound webhooks (HMAC-verified receivers, 1 MiB cap, 300s replay window) ─
# POST /api/webhooks/github  — X-Hub-Signature-256 (HMAC-SHA256, hex), X-GitHub-Delivery dedup
# POST /api/webhooks/slack   — X-Slack-Signature (v0:ts:body), X-Slack-Request-Timestamp ±300s
# Delivery IDs deduped via the webhook_delivery table. Unset secret => 503 (fail closed).
# HIVE_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# HIVE_SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET=
# HIVE_WEBHOOK_TENANT=acme           — tenant webhooks ingest into (default: acme)
# HIVE_WEBHOOK_CHANNEL=integrations  — channel quarantined inbound messages land in

# Slack (outbox effect post-slack)
# HIVE_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/T.../B.../xxx   — incoming webhook (simplest)
# HIVE_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-...      — alternative: Web API chat.postMessage
# HIVE_SLACK_CHANNEL=#bugs           — channel for Web API mode (and label in webhook mode)
# HIVE_SLACK_API_URL=https://slack.com/api          — override for tests
# HIVE_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ── Postgres 16 (cloud parity with db/migrations/001_postgres_rls.sql) ────────
# Local: docker compose up -d postgres
# Verify (throwaway db `hive_rls_verify`, drops itself afterwards):
#   HIVE_PG_ADMIN_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres \
#     npm run verify:postgres
# HIVE_PG_ADMIN_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres

# ── Frontend (static hosting, e.g. Vercel) ────────────────────────────────────
# When the React build is hosted without the Node gateway (Vercel), point the UI
# at a reachable gateway and (optionally) send the bearer token:
# VITE_HIVE_API_BASE=https://hive-gateway.example.com
# VITE_HIVE_API_TOKEN=<same value as HIVE_GATEWAY_TOKEN>
